WIFI-
you know what wifi is bro
but if you don't, no worries, AOS got you.

Wi-Fi is the invisible radio magic that lets your laptop, phone,
tablet, fridge, toaster, and probably one random smart bulb
connect to the internet without screaming through a cable.

AOS will try to support most Wi-Fi devices by version 1.0.
If your Wi-Fi card still refuses to work, then either:
1. the driver is missing
2. the hardware is cursed
3. the router has personal beef with you

Don't panic. Ethernet exists.
Yes, the ancient cable still solos sometimes.

